1
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Welcome to today's lecture on cell biology. We are going to look at what cells are made of and what each part does.

2
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:57,000
Cell theory states that all living things are made of one or more cells, that the cell is the basic unit of life, and that new cells come from existing cells.

3
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:34,000
There are two broad kinds of cell. Prokaryotic cells, such as bacteria, have no nucleus. Eukaryotic cells, such as plant and animal cells, keep their DNA inside a nucleus.

4
00:01:35,000 --> 00:02:10,000
The cell membrane is a thin, flexible barrier that controls which substances enter and leave the cell. It is partially permeable.

5
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:49,000
The nucleus is the control centre of a eukaryotic cell. It contains the genetic material, DNA, which carries the instructions for making proteins.

6
00:02:50,000 --> 00:03:33,000
Mitochondria are organelles where aerobic respiration takes place. They release energy from glucose and store it as ATP, which is why they are called the powerhouse of the cell.

7
00:03:34,000 --> 00:04:11,000
ATP, adenosine triphosphate, is the molecule cells use to carry energy to the processes that need it, such as muscle contraction and active transport.

8
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:48,000
Chloroplasts are found in plant cells and some algae. They contain chlorophyll, which absorbs light energy for photosynthesis.

9
00:04:49,000 --> 00:05:30,000
Photosynthesis is the process in which plants use light energy to convert carbon dioxide and water into glucose and oxygen.

10
00:05:31,000 --> 00:06:05,000
Ribosomes are small structures where proteins are made, following the instructions copied from DNA.

11
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:41,000
Plant cells also have a cell wall made of cellulose, which gives the cell strength and support, and a large vacuole filled with cell sap.

12
00:06:42,000 --> 00:07:12,000
To summarise: the membrane controls entry and exit, the nucleus stores DNA, mitochondria release energy as ATP, and chloroplasts carry out photosynthesis.
